/**
 * @mainpage Propositional Logic Parse Trees (CS F214, Assignment 1, Part A)
 *
 * This project stores a propositional-logic formula as a binary parse tree and runs the
 * algorithms of Tasks 1-6 on it.
 *
 * Connectives: `~` NOT, `+` OR, `*` AND, `>` implication. Input formulas are fully parenthesized.
 *
 * @section pipeline Pipeline
 * infix string --(Task 1)--> prefix string --(Task 2)--> parse tree --(Tasks 3,4,5)--> traversals,
 * height, truth value / truth table --(Task 6)--> measurements and an HTML report.
 *
 * @section files Source files
 * | Task | Files |
 * |------|-------|
 * | shared | common.h, common.cpp |
 * | 1 | task1_infix_to_prefix.h / .cpp |
 * | 2 | task2_prefix_to_tree.h / .cpp |
 * | 3 | task3_traversals.h / .cpp |
 * | 4 | task4_height.h / .cpp |
 * | 5 | task5_evaluate.h / .cpp |
 * | 6 + data set | task6_analysis.h / .cpp, dimacs.h / .cpp |
 * | driver | main.cpp |
 *
 * @section data Data set
 * DIMACS `.cnf` files of the SAT 2002 benchmark are read by readDimacs() and converted to an infix
 * formula by cnfToInfix().
 */
